# Security and approval

1. Never commit credentials, tokens, cookies, private keys, connection strings, raw .env files, or secret-bearing MCP configs.
2. Use environment variables and placeholders for secret values.
3. Prefer official integrations and minimum necessary permissions.
4. Start new external-system work with read-only discovery where practical.
5. Require explicit owner approval before production deploys, production migrations, destructive actions, DNS/routing changes, credential rotation, billing changes, purchases, or bulk outbound actions.
6. Redact sensitive values from logs, screenshots, reports, fixtures, and examples.
7. Do not treat agent instructions as the only security boundary; reinforce important controls with provider scopes, CI, branch protection, hooks, and human approval.
